<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borama</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borama is a city in the Awdal region of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, inhabited mainly by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gadabuursi">Gadabuursi</a> clan. In 1993 it hosted the Borama conference of clan elders, which adopted a national charter for Somaliland and chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-haji-ibrahim-egal">Muhammad Haji Ibrahim Egal</a> as president. It is the main town of Somaliland's western highlands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borama.jpg" alt="Borama" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mashhuur · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borama_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
